cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GateTruth, please cite it as below."
title: "GateTruth: Auditing the Rigor of RTL Design Benchmarks via Mutation Testing"
abstract: >-
  GateTruth is a mutation-testing engine and methodology for auditing the rigor of RTL benchmark
  testbenches for LLM/agent hardware design: inject deterministic, seeded semantic mutants into a
  reference implementation and measure what fraction the testbench catches. The methodology is
  validated against an included open reference suite (60 specification-to-RTL generation tasks
  and 8 agentic-repair tasks, scored through a pinned, deterministic synthesis-to-timing flow with
  correctness enforced as a strict gate) before being applied, unmodified, to external RTL
  benchmarks. 46 of the 60 Track A testbenches currently clear the suite's own >=95% mutation-kill
  floor; the other 14 do not, reported as a finding rather than omitted. See the paper for the
  exact per-task results.
type: software
